    "narrative": "For the Austin Waves on May 15, 2026, our offensive engine is centered around **Gunnar Henderson** (83.29) and **Kyle Tucker** (81.09), both of whom are clear \"Strong\" plays today. **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from an aggressive profile against Littell, buoyed by a 4.73 xERA and a high-leverage opportunity to exploit potential stolen base lanes. Similarly, **Kyle Tucker** is in a prime position against Kochanowicz; with the opponent's poor SP_xERA (5.19) and a 19% boost from SP skill factors, he is our most reliable source of counting stats today. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.62) also merits attention as a high-upside play, leveraging a strong platoon advantage against Baz to bolster our efficiency.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today was keeping **Coby Mayo** (50.72) on the bench. While he carries significant power potential, his projected efficiency fell just short of our utility threshold compared to **Brady House** (56.80). **Brady House** gets the edge here due to a favorable matchup against Baz and the added bonus of a slow pitcher delivery, which elevates his stolen base potential\u2014a critical factor given our emphasis on speed scarcity. Meanwhile, **Drake Baldwin** faces the toughest challenge of our starters, with his score suppressed to 47.27 due to an elite 2.92 xERA from Early, making him a marginal play we are monitoring closely.\n\nWe are keeping a watchful eye on **Josh Lowe** (53.72) and **Sam Antonacci** (51.17), both of whom hover near our floor for starts. While **Sam Antonacci** benefits from a lead-off spot against Cabrera, his overall projection remains modest. Conversely, **Heliot Ramos** (64.04) and **Andy Pages** (67.92) round out a robust outfield, with **Heliot Ramos** specifically benefiting from a park-factor boost that outweighs his neutral platoon status. Aside from monitoring late-arriving lineup confirmations, our primary concern remains the high-skill pitching of Early, which complicates the start for **Drake Baldwin**, but overall, the Waves are positioned to capitalize on favorable park conditions and weak opposing rotations.",
